A macro declared as a real argv command in the global config executes through the CLI
subprocess: the command's own output lands in the frontmatter, and nothing could have
produced it but the run.

-- fixtures/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
status: backlog
---
# My Plan

- [ ] 3 SP: Task one
- [ ] 2 SP: Task two
-- fixtures/xdg/booping/config.yaml --
core:
  macros:
    count: ["echo", "1"]
-- cmd --
booping frontmatter-update plan.md attempts="{{ macro('core.macros.count') }}"
-- exit --
0
-- stdout --
--- plan.md
+++ plan.md
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 ---
 title: Foo
 status: backlog
+attempts: 1
 ---
 # My Plan
 
-- stderr --
updated plan.md: attempts=1
-- expected/cwd/plan.md --
---
title: Foo
status: backlog
attempts: 1
---
# My Plan

- [ ] 3 SP: Task one
- [ ] 2 SP: Task two
